# Rust
/target
*.part

# Local build caches from Build.bat: several GB each, never published.
#   target-fast  -> `Build.bat fast`  (no LTO, all cores)
#   target-bench -> `Build.bat bench` (profile comparison)
/target-fast
/target-bench

# Locally built binaries
Todo Downloader.exe
Todo Downloader (test).exe

# IDE
/.idea
/.vscode

# Local animations for the support tab: never published (third-party GIFs).
# The README stays, so anyone cloning the repo learns what the folder is for.
/tips/*
!/tips/README.txt

# Release artwork: goes in the Releases page and the social preview, not here.
todo-downloader-banner-*.png

# Release descriptions: they go in the GitHub Releases page, not in the repo.
GITHUB-RELEASE-TEXT-*.md
COMMIT-*.txt

# Architecture decision records: reasoning kept locally, not published.
ADR-*.md

# Internal working notes: implementation reasoning, not user documentation.
# Kept locally, never published.
MEGA-IMPLEMENTATION-DECISION.md
MEGA-FEASIBILITY.md

# Local build helpers. The documented way to build is `cargo build --release`,
# so per-machine scripts stay out of the repository.
*.bat
